stage: 2
finding: A copied example is not verified as its own installed project, and it fails a supported isolated install: I packed HEAD, installed that tarball in a temporary project, copied loading-screen with the installed shallot add, pointed the copied manifest at the same local tarball, then ran bun install --linker isolated in the copied example. Its node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc -p tsconfig.json failed with TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for '@webgpu/types'. The exported tsconfig.base.json includes @webgpu/types in compilerOptions.types, but the generated example manifest does not declare it; isolated linking keeps Shallot's transitive dependency out of the example's type lookup. The committed packed-install test misses this because it installs TypeScript, Vite, TypeGPU and Bun types on the scratch project's parent manifest, runs tools from that parent node_modules, never installs the copied example, and its generated TGSL test imports typegpu without that example declaring it. Thus parent dependencies mask the copied manifest's actual install shape.
